# PLAN-1082 — AV 数组、集合语法与嵌套 place（语言共享语料 collections 面）

The canonical author of the collections-and-places language family.
Every case carries ONE Auto source; the `av` check runs the ordinary AV
language chain (`ac-av/language-source-run-v1`); legacy `VM result`
checks keep their original oracles and owners with the AV-phase
`#ignore` marker (AV-ONLY-1078-1096) — not executed in this phase, never
blocking the AV gate; their backend tasks remove the marker when they
land.

Auditable normalizations (recorded per row in
`language/migration/legacy-map.tsv`, same policy as PLAN-1080's
`double`→`twice` and PLAN-1081's typed-lambda annotations):

- Legacy script-top programs (`[1, 2, 3]` as the trailing value) wrap in
  `fn main` and observe through typed exits/prints — the legacy display
  oracle stays the row's original oracle in the map.
- Legacy lambdas were untyped (`x =>`); the canonical spellings carry
  `int` annotations (no lambda parameter inference on this face).
- Legacy `List.new()` (zero args) and `[]` have no element-type
  inference site — the canonical spelling is `List<int>.new()` (oracles
  only observe len/emptiness); the zero-arg sugar keeps a NAMED
  rejection.
- Legacy `list.drop()` cleanup is scope-exit release on the checked face
  (omitted); `is_empty()` is `len() == 0`; `pop()` prints through the
  Option `is Some` unwrap (the frozen stdlib pop keeps None-not-trap);
  `contains(v)` rides the real 972 `find` family; `for_each` is a plain
  `for` (not in the 972 assembled set); `reserve` (unobservable capacity
  pre-allocation) is dropped with the len oracle intact.
- Legacy negative indexing (`a[-1]` = from-end) keeps the frozen SEM-02
  approved difference: negative subscripts trap `av.trap.list-index`
  like every other out-of-domain index — the legacy from-end oracle is a
  difference account, never a green oracle.

