## Case: list-ops-family
id: "av.parity.1082.list-ops-family"
tags: ["av-language-parity", "plan-1082", "collections"]
links: ["PLAN-1082"]
entry-mode: "program"

### Auto
path: "main.at"

```auto
fn main() {
 var list = List<int>.new()
 print(list.len())
 list.push(10)
 list.push(20)
 list.push(30)
 print(list.len())
 print(list.get(1))
 print(list[1])
 list.set(1, 99)
 print(list.get(1))
 list.set(1, 20)
 var popped = 0
 let p = list.pop()
 is p { Some(v) -> { popped = v } None -> { popped = 0 } }
 print(popped)
 print(list.len())
 list.insert(1, 55)
 var v = list.get(1)
 list.remove(1)
 print(v)
 print(list.len())
 list.clear()
 print(list.len())
}
```

### Probe av
recipe: "ac-av/language-source-run-v1"
entry: "d_main"
caps: ["ac.source.language.av/v1", "console.stdout", "console.stderr"]
channel: "unit"

#### stdout

```text
0
3
20
20
99
30
2
55
2
0
```

### Notes

legacy.13_collections.020/021/022/023/025/026/027/028/029/030/031 —
the List ops family, original oracle digits preserved: empty len 0
(.020/.029 e1), len 3 (.023), get(1) 20 (.030 v), bare index 20 (.031),
set+get 99 (.030 v2), pop 30 (.021), len-after-pop 2 (.022 len2),
insert/get/remove 55 then len 2 (.027), clear len 0 (.025/.029 e2);
.028's reserve (capacity pre-allocation, unobservable) drops with its
len-2 oracle intact; `.drop()` normalizes to scope-exit release.
legacy.13_collections.026's display oracle '[10, 99, 30]' is the row's
original oracle in the map (its three values print as digits here).

